## Intuition
Comparing bit by bit till both numbers become zeros.

## Approach
Use a while loop to iterate through till the `start` and `goal` become zeros and for every iteration check if bits are opposite, if so increase the count.

## Solution
```java[]
class Solution {
    public int minBitsFlip(int start, int goal) {
        int ans = 0;
        while(start != goal) {
            if(start % 2 != goal % 2) ans++;
            start = start >> 1;
            goal = goal >> 1;
        }

        return ans;
    }
}
```

## Complexity
**Time Complexity:** 
O(1) as while loop doesn't go beyond int (32 or 64 depends on OS) size.

**Space Complexity:**
O(1) as we are using variables to store data.
